  "cutout_from": "Not declared. spider01, the legs, is the .OZT of the pair with a hard alpha mask (59% fully solid); `cutout` would key the mask off brightness instead, and on dark bristles over a dark ground that left the legs as orange confetti (the rebuild of 2026-10-12 found `mu new` declaring it again). Left off, the sheet's own alpha is used and the export is still alpha-tested.",
  "maps": 1024,
  "maps_from": "Not MU's: 33 of the 39 islands are leg cards that each sample the whole 32x64 hair sheet, so the 192 the widest-sheet rule gives left each leg about 30 of its 96 pixels and rendered as speckles. 1024 holds every island at exactly 3x its own art (about 682k texels of content).",
  "material_overrides": {
    "chitin": {
      "roughness": 0.85
    }
  },
  "material_overrides_from": "The user's, 2026-10-11: 'spiders boddy has glossy effect which does not make sense'. Chitin's 0.62 lit a white sheen across the back at noon; this spider is small and hairy and MU painted its shading in.",
